{
  "summary": "Fixes several socket-chunking and handshake edge cases in the functional test framework's v1 and v2 P2P parsing. P2PConnection now waits for the full 24-byte header before checking v1 magic bytes, properly tracks handshake completion when garbage length is zero, correctly returns per-call consumed byte counts in respond_v2_handshake(), and handles partial ellswift reads gracefully in p2p_v2_misbehaving.py.",
  "problem": "When socket reads arrive in small chunks or when randomized handshake parameters hit edge cases (such as zero-length garbage or partial ellswift reads), functional tests like p2p_v2_encrypted.py and p2p_v2_misbehaving.py can desync, crash with index errors, or hang indefinitely waiting for handshakes.",
